  "body": "In IRC @sicking and I went in circles for a bit over the confusion between \"buffer\" as in ArrayBuffer (i.e. continuous chunk of memory, often one of the things in your stream) and \"buffer\" as in \"the stream's collection of so-far buffered chunks.\"\n\nI am wondering if anyone else thinks this is confusing and if so should we rename the spec's \"buffer\" concept to something like \"queue\" to avoid such confusion in the future.\n\nIf we do keep \"buffer\" we should be explicit pretty early in the spec about what that means and how we use it.\n",
